  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14222207/assets/eba7dd6d571c989a14900a91eb432a216b74717046bfaa19e5fbe4de7abe6503.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\theta ={20}^{∘}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{20}^{∘}=0.939\\,69…≈0.94.\n$$",
